The provided test code has a latent bug where it does not correctly handle the `-ENOSYS` error code from the second GPIO direction check in each test case. This could lead to a test failure instead of a skip when a driver implements the `get_direction` callback but returns `-ENOSYS` for one of the direction queries. Additionally, one of the test cases has a misleading comment.

The fix is to refactor all test cases to perform both direction checks first, then check for `-ENOSYS` from either call, and only then assert the expected outcomes. This makes the tests more robust and corrects the misleading comment.

